====================================================================================
THE CATALAN LAW:  A_{2k} = C_k p^{k+1} + O(p^{k+1/2})   (sharpening HYP-2307)
====================================================================================
Catalan C_1..C_5 = [1, 2, 5, 14, 42]

L=4 (k=2): A_4/p^3 -> C_2 = 2
    p |          A_4 |   A_4/p^3 | (2-A_4/p^3)*sqrt p
    7 |          336 |   0.97959 |             2.6997
   11 |         1760 |   1.32231 |             2.2476
   19 |        10944 |   1.59557 |             1.7629
   23 |        20240 |   1.66352 |             1.6137
   31 |        52080 |   1.74818 |             1.4021
   43 |       144480 |   1.81720 |             1.1987
   47 |       190256 |   1.83250 |             1.1483
   59 |       383264 |   1.86613 |             1.0283
   67 |       566016 |   1.88193 |             0.9664

L=6 (k=3): A_6/p^4 -> C_3 = 5  (subleading O(p^{3.5}) oscillates in sign)
    p |            A_6 |   A_6/p^4
    7 |           1008 |   0.41983
   11 |          22880 |   1.56273
   19 |         361152 |   2.77125
   23 |         870320 |   3.11005

L=8 (k=4): A_8/p^5 -> C_4 = 14
    p |              A_8 |   A_8/p^5
    7 |                0 |   0.00000
   11 |           154880 |   0.96168

=> A_{2k}/p^{2k} -> 0 for all k>=2 (since k+1<2k); only a_2=1 survives; R(p)->e.
